gpu: the window's text drawn by the gpu

a run of text is made an image on the cpu, freetype's glyphs blended on
its ground, and gio shows it pixel for pixel
(`gio/ft.go:/a run is made here/`). a terminal in the window redraws
its grid as fast as a program writes: the glyphs kept on the gpu once,
in a texture, and each cell drawn from it, would leave the cpu out.
later, when a measure says the cpu is where the time goes.
